WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.510
Un, Deux, Trois, Cat! The dexterity game where you grab cat toys.

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:08.610
And you can learn it in seconds, so everyone plays at once,

3
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.450
and nobody's waiting for a turn.

4
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:16.080
Every toy has its own color: yellow bird, green fish, blue ball, and so on.

5
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:20.830
Cards show every toy in every color. See one in its own color?

6
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.190
Grab it. No matching colors? Grab the cat.

7
00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.100
Here's how a round works:

8
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:31.780
everybody chants un, deux, trois, cat, and on cat, everybody flips.

9
00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:35.670
Nothing's in its own color here, so Gato grabs the cat.

10
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:39.310
The green fish: its own color. I grab it.

11
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.910
Two right answers? Each is a point, and I'm fast enough to take both.

12
00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.020
Decoys can lure you in.

13
00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:52.120
Gato grabs the wrong color fish and loses a point. The answer was the cat.

14
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.120
Every flip is a scramble:

15
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.030
hands collide over the toys, and the whole table's shouting.

16
00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:01.500
And the decoys get everyone eventually, so nobody stops at just one game.

17
00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.870
Six cat toys and sixty cards.

18
00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:08.070
Two to six players, in about ten minutes. Most points wins.

19
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.690
Or try the Cat Paw edition:

20
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.940
everyone bats the toys towards themselves with a cat paw on a stick.

21
00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.160
Un, Deux, Trois, Cat!

22
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.500
Play in your browser at darrendon.com, or email me for a prototype.
